-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- floats: bits
-- The primitives give Float64 arithmetic and comparison, Float64 ↔ Int64, and the bits of both
-- formats; there is no Float32 arithmetic and no conversion between the formats. Both are
-- written here on the bits: fp-pack rounds an integer magnitude times a power of two to the
-- nearest value of a format (ties to even), which is every conversion into a format; binary32
-- arithmetic is then binary64's on the widened operands, narrowed (one rounding of the exact
-- result, since 53 ≥ 2·24 + 2).
uq-bl-step : UInt64 → DQ → DQ
uq-bl-step k s = case uq-iszero (u64shr (fst s) k) of
  true → s
  false → (u64shr (fst s) k , u64add (snd s) k)
